1
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:09,901
This is Kipdeck, built on agent-office.

2
00:00:10,151 --> 00:00:13,191
Every coding agent is a unit at a console.

3
00:00:13,441 --> 00:00:16,165
The office ranks who needs you first:

4
00:00:16,415 --> 00:00:19,139
needs you, stuck, to review, working.

5
00:00:19,389 --> 00:00:22,050
Every screen reads that one ranking.

6
00:00:22,850 --> 00:00:25,381
Issue two on our public demo repo

7
00:00:25,631 --> 00:00:28,486
holds 15 test tokens on Solana devnet,

8
00:00:28,736 --> 00:00:31,527
in a vault only the program can move.

9
00:00:31,777 --> 00:00:34,307
Anyone can fund it from the board

10
00:00:34,557 --> 00:00:37,413
or a Blink, signing with their wallet.

11
00:00:37,663 --> 00:00:39,869
Here a unit is hired for it.

12
00:00:40,119 --> 00:00:42,650
It works in its own git worktree.

13
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:45,591
The new unit is already at work.

14
00:00:45,841 --> 00:00:48,152
Here's one a unit finished earlier:

15
00:00:48,402 --> 00:00:49,923
PR #4, for issue one.

16
00:00:50,173 --> 00:00:52,371
It was opened on the repo itself.

17
00:00:52,621 --> 00:00:54,650
A PR from a fork never counts.

18
00:00:55,450 --> 00:00:57,477
When a person merges, the office

19
00:00:57,727 --> 00:01:00,233
asks GitHub: merged by a user, not a bot,

20
00:01:00,483 --> 00:01:02,670
with write access? PR #4 was merged

21
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:05,107
by its own operator: labelled self,

22
00:01:05,357 --> 00:01:07,650
so it paid nothing. This is a replay.

23
00:01:08,450 --> 00:01:10,238
Even then, nothing pays yet.

24
00:01:10,488 --> 00:01:12,696
The payout waits in the review inbox

25
00:01:12,946 --> 00:01:14,628
until an admin approves it

26
00:01:14,878 --> 00:01:17,244
with a signature from their own wallet,

27
00:01:17,494 --> 00:01:19,650
so no key on the server pays alone.

28
00:01:20,450 --> 00:01:23,844
On a counted merge, the bounty pays out.

29
00:01:24,094 --> 00:01:27,340
Here's a real release from a test run,

30
00:01:27,590 --> 00:01:30,320
with no GitHub merge behind it.

31
00:01:30,570 --> 00:01:32,857
It needed two signatures:

32
00:01:33,107 --> 00:01:35,763
the attester and the approver.

33
00:01:36,013 --> 00:01:39,259
The program is native Rust, no Anchor.

34
00:01:39,509 --> 00:01:42,755
Release fails unless both have signed.

35
00:01:43,005 --> 00:01:46,252
Both keys are in the bounty's address,

36
00:01:46,502 --> 00:01:49,526
so a bounty can't swap its signers.

37
00:01:49,776 --> 00:01:53,096
After expiry, anyone can send a refund,

38
00:01:53,346 --> 00:01:56,150
and it goes back to each funder.

39
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:59,123
Every counted merge is also attested

40
00:01:59,373 --> 00:02:00,977
on Base Sepolia with EAS.

41
00:02:01,227 --> 00:02:03,141
Reputation lives on Base, where

42
00:02:03,391 --> 00:02:05,150
the ERC-8004 registries are.

43
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:08,409
The board at slash pom is rebuilt

44
00:02:08,659 --> 00:02:10,425
from chain data alone.

45
00:02:10,675 --> 00:02:12,882
Every row links to its proof.

46
00:02:13,132 --> 00:02:15,150
Shown here with test data.

47
00:02:15,950 --> 00:02:18,459
Outsiders can pay for one task with x402.

48
00:02:18,709 --> 00:02:20,578
The first request gets a 402.

49
00:02:20,828 --> 00:02:23,391
This test payment settled on Base Sepolia.

50
00:02:23,641 --> 00:02:26,150
The task is held until an admin approves.

51
00:02:26,950 --> 00:02:29,384
Repos can skip the office entirely:

52
00:02:29,634 --> 00:02:32,306
this Action runs the same merge checks.

53
00:02:32,556 --> 00:02:35,169
So far only against a test GitHub API.

54
00:02:35,419 --> 00:02:38,150
It's pinned to a commit: it holds a key.

55
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:41,684
Testnet keys sit in owner-only files,

56
00:02:41,934 --> 00:02:44,032
and workers never see them.

57
00:02:44,282 --> 00:02:47,016
Nothing is audited yet: testnet only.

58
00:02:47,266 --> 00:02:50,191
Everything on chain is new in this fork.

59
00:02:50,441 --> 00:02:52,793
It's MIT, built on agent-office

60
00:02:53,043 --> 00:02:55,650
by webdevcody. Thanks for watching.
